  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "A bounded non-one-hot policy target built from paired common-random-number all-legal action advantages, with uncertainty-conservative LCB targets and row-only reliability weighting, will provide lower-variance alternative-action supervision and improve robust policy strength without the chosen-action Q bias that failed historically.",
  "material_change": "First decouple policy-only counterfactual distillation from the Action-Q head so no Q values enter rollout action selection. Build one immutable balanced BB/SB x flop/turn dataset by strictly merging the existing 10,240-row paired-CRN partial dataset with its 512-row SB-turn shard. Relative to the untouched all-heads control, enable only bounded soft-policy replay at coefficient 0.01, advantage_lcb z=1.96, row_only reliability, one 512-row replay batch per update, and linear decay to zero over 262,144 hands. Keep lambda 0.95 and all other control seeds, deals, league, architecture, and PPO settings.",
  "baseline": "adaptive-league-all-heads-pilot-20260830 untouched on-policy all-policy-heads control",
  "source": "Legacy exact Action-Q and one-step hard/capped selectors failed, but the current paired-uncertainty loader and bounded soft-policy objective provide a distinct conservative all-legal target; the available partial data plus SB-turn shard cover all four seat/street cells and five trajectory styles.",
  "parent_id": "monte-carlo-gae-pilot-20260830",
